From 5dd105ba5a827538cf4c09da00d6decad3484fa7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:45:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] GS6: AirSky::Chip lays the clouds' float table; the chip
 test checks every point the chip draws against the painter's

The Chip gathers the puffs as the Painter does (with a 400 m margin), orders them far to near, and lays 8 texels a puff
in a float table; Battle/AirSkyChip.inl turns each point from it. Tools/air_show/air_sky_chip_test.cpp compiles the
same .inl as C++ and checks the ground's two skies and the three recordings: 1,263,372 points, 0.010 m at most apart,
colour within 1 of 255; a table read anywhere within its slack equals a fresh lay. Not yet wired into the scene.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L4rhyzzCJpbk7hzRiikzLD
